    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0285" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg205"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-02-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 503.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instruction No. 526
                    of the 7th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a note from
                    Lord Lansdowne, in which it is stated that His Majesty’s Government will have
                    pleasure in acceding to the wish of our Government that His Majesty’s consul at
                    Boma may be authorized to take charge of American interests in the Kongo Free
                    State until such time as consular representatives can be provided for by action
                    of the Congress of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d190-a1.xml" xpointer="d190-a1"/>
